# default.pgo capture manifest

Regenerate with the procedure in sdk/docs/architecture.md, "Build Profiles and
Observable Runtime". Update this file in the same change set as default.pgo.

    revision:   569c5ec1
    toolchain:  go1.26.4 linux/amd64
    host CPU:   Intel(R) Xeon(R) W-11955M CPU @ 2.60GHz
    captured:   2026-07-22
    capture:    IE_CPUPROFILE=<path> on a `go build -pgo=off` binary
    merge:      go tool pprof -proto <profiles...> > default.pgo

## Workloads

| Profile              | Duration | Command                                                                          |
|----------------------|----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| compositor_rotozoomer| 30 s     | -ie64 sdk/examples/prebuilt/rotozoomer_ie64.ie64                                   |
| voodoo_megademo      | 30 s     | -ie32 sdk/examples/prebuilt/voodoo_mega_demo.iex                                   |
| audio_wav            | 30 s     | -wav DoctorWhoSID.wav                                                              |
| emutos_desktop       | 35 s     | -emutos -emutos-image sdk/examples/prebuilt/etos256us.img                          |
| iescript_emutos      | 15 s     | -emutos -emutos-image sdk/examples/prebuilt/etos256us.img -script emutos_jit_probe.ies |
| robocop_m68k         | 30 s     | -m68k sdk/examples/prebuilt/robocop_intro_68k.ie68                                 |

The IEScript workload ends when the script calls sys.exit, so its duration is
shorter than the timeout used to bound it.

## Acceptance

`go build -pgo=default.pgo .` completes with no warning and no fallback.

benchstat over BenchmarkComposite_*, BenchmarkVoodoo_FullFrame,
